00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:29.510
And then Jan calls on speakerphone.
然后简用免提打了电话过来。

486
00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:35.110
And do we find out Michael's nickname for her in this moment?
我们是在这一刻发现迈克尔给她的昵称吗？

487
00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:36.010
What does he call her?
他叫她什么？

488
00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.370
He says, hello, Buttercup.
他说，你好，毛茛花。

489
00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:39.770
Oh.
噢。

490
00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.670
Is this a Princess Bride moment?
这是在致敬《公主新娘》吗？

491
00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:43.090
It sounds like it.
听起来像是。

492
00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:43.850
A little bit.
有点像。

493
00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:53.370
Well, Jan is like, what do you say we blow off this party and we just, like, we just go after each other like we did on that black sand beach in Jamaica?
简说，我们不去参加这个派对了，我们就像在牙买加那片黑沙滩上那样，好好亲热一番怎么样？

494
00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:53.950
Yeah.
没错。

495
00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:58.410
Doesn't she say something like, why don't we just smash up on each other or something?
她是不是说了类似“我们为什么不直接滚床单”之类的话？

496
00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:01.150
It's a real visual image I probably didn't need.
那画面感太强了，我其实并不想看到。

497
00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:04.210
And then she's like, wait, am I on speakerphone?
然后她说，等等，我是在用免提吗？

498
00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:05.930
Are the cameras there?
摄像机在那儿吗？

499
00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:07.830
And she's like, I'll just see you at the party.
接着她说，那派对上见吧。

500
00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:11.430
But Michael does not want to go get it on with Jan.
但迈克尔其实并不想和简亲热。

501
00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:17.870
He is like, no, I want to go to this party with you and show everyone that you and I are together.
他就像是说，不，我想和你一起去参加这个派对，向大家展示我们在一起了。

502
00:22:18.250 --> 00:22:18.790
I know.
我知道。

503
00:22:18.990 --> 00:22:22.430
This kind of breaks my heart because it's clearly so important for him.
这让我有点心碎，因为这对他来说显然非常重要。

504
00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:24.870
And she just wants to blow it off.
而她却只想敷衍了事。

505
00:22:25.090 --> 00:22:27.230
She doesn't want to go public with him.
她不想公开他们两人的关系。

506
00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:29.230
And he's kind of forcing her hand.
而他有点在强迫她做决定。

507
00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:34.830
And Jan, I know you're a fictional character and you won't ever hear this, but I need to say it.
还有简，我知道你是个虚构角色，永远听不到这些，但我必须得说出来。

508
00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:39.930
Always assume you're on speakerphone and cameras are rolling.
永远要假设自己正处于免提通话状态，而且摄像机正在拍摄。

509
00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:43.310
This is something that comes up with her all the time.
这事儿在她身上总是发生。

510
00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:44.670
She's like, are the cameras there?
她会问，摄像机在那儿吗？

511
00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:46.090
I'm like, why are you asking?
我就说，你问这个干嘛？

512
00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:47.750
Just give up.
放弃吧。

513
00:22:47.890 --> 00:22:48.510
They're there.
它们就在那儿。

514
00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:50.370
It's so true.
太真实了。

515
00:22:51.150 --> 00:22:59.390
Well, then Jenna, as they're off and on their way, we have at front reception, Roy and Pam.
好吧，那么珍娜，当他们准备出发时，前台那边是罗伊和帕姆。

516
00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:03.050
And Pam was like, Roy, come out with us tonight.
帕姆说，罗伊，今晚跟我们一起出去吧。

517
00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:06.570
And he's like, no, my brother took a bath on the jet skis.
他说，不行，我兄弟在摩托艇上亏了一大笔钱。

518
00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:07.810
We're going to go get drunk.
我们要去喝个烂醉。

519
00:23:07.810 --> 00:23:11.050
And you're like, yeah, we're going to a bar.
而你就像是说，没错，我们要去酒吧。

520
00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:13.950
We're going somewhere where that can happen.
我们要去一个能喝醉的地方。

521
00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:15.410
And you've got to do boyfriend stuff.
你得尽到男朋友的责任。

522
00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:16.770
If you want to be my boyfriend, right?
如果你想做我男朋友的话，对吧？

523
00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:17.950
You make a big speech.
你得发表一番慷慨陈词。

524
00:23:18.730 --> 00:23:18.910
Yeah.
没错。

525
00:23:19.110 --> 00:23:20.650
And Roy is like, OK.
然后罗伊说，好吧。

526
00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:21.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

527
00:23:21.850 --> 00:23:27.230
And it's kind of this nice moment where you see Pam is being more assertive and Roy hears her.
这是一个挺温馨的时刻，你看到帕姆变得更果断了，而罗伊也听进去了。

528
00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:31.390
Well, there's a deleted scene, Jenna, that would have happened right here that I thought was really
嗯，珍娜，这里本来有一个删减片段，我觉得真的很温馨，

529
00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:36.270
sweet, where Roy notices your art has been framed and is hanging on the wall.
罗伊注意到你的画被装裱起来挂在墙上了。

530
00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:37.470
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

531
00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:38.470
And he compliments it.
他还夸奖了它。

532
00:23:38.530 --> 00:23:40.850
He's like, hey, oh, my God, it's your art.
他说，嘿，天哪，这是你的画。

533
00:23:41.010 --> 00:23:42.010
It's framed.
装裱起来了。

534
00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:43.630
You know, that's so cool.
你知道，这太酷了。

535
00:23:43.630 --> 00:23:49.230
And it's this sweet moment that I think would have just extended that beat of where Roy,
这是一个很温馨的时刻，我觉得它本可以延伸罗伊的那个片段，

536
00:23:49.230 --> 00:23:50.530
he's trying.
他是在努力。

537
00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:51.410
Yeah.
没错。

538
00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:57.430
Before we move on from the sweet Pam Roy moment, there is a new plant alert.
在我们离开帕姆和罗伊这个温馨时刻之前，有个新植物警报。

539
00:23:57.810 --> 00:24:00.190
Another new plant at reception?
前台又有新植物了？

540
00:24:00.530 --> 00:24:07.230
I wish really and truly there was a way that someone could, by the end of the nine years,
我真心希望在九年结束时，能有人告诉我们，

541
00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:09.990
tell us how many plants that Pam had had.
帕姆到底养过多少盆植物。

542
00:24:10.290 --> 00:24:11.710
There is a new plant.
确实有一盆新植物。

543
00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:18.890
It's in a very cute blue ceramic pot with what looks like to be like little colorful balloons on the pot.
它在一个非常可爱的蓝色陶瓷花盆里，盆上看起来像是画着彩色的小气球。

544
00:24:19.230 --> 00:24:19.930
Hmm.
嗯。

545
00:24:20.330 --> 00:24:21.210
It's very cute.
非常可爱。

546
00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:22.730
It won't laSt.
它活不长。

547
00:24:23.130 --> 00:24:24.310
It's very cute.
非常可爱。

548
00:24:25.610 --> 00:24:32.770
My gosh, what is this like secret story we're telling about Pam's ability to care for house plants?
天哪，我们到底在讲一个关于帕姆养植物能力的什么秘密故事？

549
00:24:33.110 --> 00:24:34.870
Well, it's not much of a story.
嗯，这算不上什么故事。

550
00:24:36.410 --> 00:24:40.710
You know, a friend of mine gave me an air plant recently.
你知道，最近有个朋友送了我一盆空气凤梨。

551
00:24:41.250 --> 00:24:42.870
It lives on air.
它靠空气生存。

552
00:24:43.310 --> 00:24:46.630
You like water it once a week.
你每周给它浇一次水。

553
00:24:46.630 --> 00:24:51.950
You turn it upside down and you put it in a glass of water and then you put it back in the pot.
你把它倒过来放进一杯水里，然后再放回盆子里。

554
00:24:52.350 --> 00:24:53.690
And you know what, Angela?
你知道吗，安吉拉？

555
00:24:54.270 --> 00:24:55.030
It's dead.
它死了。

556
00:24:55.350 --> 00:24:57.130
Well, it doesn't sound like a real thing.
嗯，听起来不像真的。

557
00:24:57.410 --> 00:24:57.810
What?
什么？

558
00:24:57.930 --> 00:24:58.630
No, it's real.
不，它是真的。

559
00:24:58.770 --> 00:25:00.030
An air plant is real.
空气凤梨是真的。

560
00:25:00.310 --> 00:25:01.470
It's a real thing.
它是真实存在的东西。

561
00:25:01.470 --> 00:25:03.550
It was living in air.
它之前靠空气活着。

562
00:25:03.690 --> 00:25:05.570
It's not even in any soil.
它甚至都不需要土壤。

563
00:25:05.810 --> 00:25:07.330
What do you mean in air?
什么叫靠空气活着？

564
00:25:07.510 --> 00:25:09.030
What does that even look like?
那到底长什么样？

565
00:25:09.250 --> 00:25:10.670
It looks like a plant.
它看起来就像株植物。

566
00:25:10.670 --> 00:25:16.570
It's in a piece of wood, but there's no soil or water in the pot.
它长在一块木头上，但盆里没有土也没有水。

567
00:25:16.850 --> 00:25:17.170
Okay?
懂了吗？

568
00:25:18.030 --> 00:25:20.610
It's like a ferny kind of plant.
它就像是一种蕨类植物。

569
00:25:20.630 --> 00:25:21.230
Okay.
好吧。

570
00:25:21.470 --> 00:25:22.270
And then you...
然后你……

571
00:25:22.270 --> 00:25:29.670
The idea is that this is the thing that people who can't keep other plants alive can keep alive because it lives on air.
它的理念是，那些养不活其他植物的人也能养活它，因为它靠空气生存。

572
00:25:29.670 --> 00:25:30.550
I don't know.
我不知道。

573
00:25:30.850 --> 00:25:32.390
But mine is dead.
但我的那株死了。

574
00:25:32.670 --> 00:25:34.230
Is it like a fancy chia pet?
它就像那种花哨的奇亚宠物吗？

575
00:25:35.370 --> 00:25:36.730
No, no.
不，不是。

576
00:25:37.570 --> 00:25:39.010
It's an air plant.
它是空气凤梨。

577
00:25:40.050 --> 00:25:41.750
It was an air plant.
它曾经是株空气凤梨。

578
00:25:41.750 --> 00:25:42.810
It was.
确实是。

579
00:25:43.110 --> 00:25:44.310
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

580
00:25:44.470 --> 00:25:46.490
You and Pam can't keep plants alive.
你和帕姆都养不活植物。

581
00:25:46.770 --> 00:25:47.830
We can't.
我们确实养不活。

582
00:25:48.370 --> 00:25:49.330
Well, listen.
好吧，听着。

583
00:25:49.570 --> 00:25:53.690
Pam is now going to have her big moment in her talking head.
帕姆现在要在她的访谈环节迎来高光时刻了。

584
00:25:53.830 --> 00:25:55.050
All right, everyone?
大家都准备好了吗？

585
00:25:55.290 --> 00:25:57.550
She is going to start being direct with people.
她要开始直接面对大家了。

586
00:25:57.850 --> 00:26:00.550
She's going to start asking for what she wants.
她要开始争取她想要的东西了。

587
00:26:00.550 --> 00:26:04.850
She says, look out, world, old Pammy is getting what she wants.
她说，世界，小心了，老帕米要得到她想要的东西了。

588
00:26:05.550 --> 00:26:07.390
And don't call me Pammy.
还有，别叫我帕米。

589
00:26:07.750 --> 00:26:08.250
Yeah.
是啊。

590
00:26:08.970 --> 00:26:10.810
I get that quoted to me a lot.
这句话经常有人引用给我听。

591
00:26:11.130 --> 00:26:11.930
Do you really?
真的吗？

592
00:26:12.410 --> 00:26:12.630
Yeah.
真的。

593
00:26:12.770 --> 00:26:13.950
And don't call me Pammy.
还有，别叫我帕米。

594
00:26:14.150 --> 00:26:16.430
The things people quote to us are so different.
人们引用给我们的东西真是大不相同。

595
00:26:16.710 --> 00:26:17.790
Like, I get poop.
比如，我收到的是关于屎的。

596
00:26:18.030 --> 00:26:19.170
It's raining from the ceilings.
天花板上在下屎。

597
00:26:19.370 --> 00:26:19.770
Poop.
屎。

598
00:26:20.190 --> 00:26:25.350
Well, we had a fan question from Ashley Portugal and Stephanie Shipman Barani.
好吧，我们有一个来自阿什莉·葡萄牙和斯蒂芬妮·希普曼·巴拉尼的粉丝提问。

599
00:26:25.350 --> 00:26:31.210
In this episode, when Pam decides she's going to be more assertive and she says, and don't
在这一集中，当帕姆决定要变得更自信，她说“还有，别”

600
00:26:31.210 --> 00:26:35.390
call me Pammy, it kind of leads us to believe that she doesn't like that nickname.
“叫我帕米”时，这让我们觉得她不喜欢那个绰号。

601
00:26:35.630 --> 00:26:41.190
But in the next episode, when Roy and Pam are talking at the diner, he calls her Pammy.
但在下一集中，当罗伊和帕姆在餐馆聊天时，他叫她“帕米”。

602
00:26:42.050 --> 00:26:46.810
Do you think that was a way of showing how Roy doesn't really know or pay much attention
你觉得这是在表现罗伊其实并不了解帕姆，或者说不太关注

603
00:26:46.810 --> 00:26:49.070
to Pam and her likes and dislikes?
帕姆的喜好吗？

604
00:26:49.930 --> 00:26:50.530
Yeah.
是啊。

605
00:26:51.030 --> 00:26:57.650
I think this is planting the seed for this nickname of Pammy that she's probably said,
我觉得这是在为“帕米”这个昵称埋下伏笔，她可能说过，

606
00:26:57.910 --> 00:26:59.950
I don't love that nickname.
我不喜欢那个昵称。

607
00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:03.630
And he just is the guy who's like, oh, whatever.
而他就是那种觉得“哦，无所谓啦”的人。

608
00:27:03.890 --> 00:27:05.210
Tickle, tickle, Pammy.
挠挠痒，帕米。

609
00:27:05.470 --> 00:27:06.010
Yeah.
是啊。

610
00:27:06.070 --> 00:27:07.850
And you're like, no, I actually mean it.
然后你会觉得，不，我是认真的。

611
00:27:07.970 --> 00:27:10.690
Like, I really don't like being called Pammy.
我是说，我真的不喜欢被叫帕米。

612
00:27:10.830 --> 00:27:12.490
And he's like, okay, Pammy.
而他却说，好的，帕米。

613
00:27:12.710 --> 00:27:12.930
Yeah.
是啊。

614
00:27:13.650 --> 00:27:14.090
Right?
对吧？

615
00:27:14.330 --> 00:27:16.090
And then you just give up.
然后你就放弃了。

616
00:27:16.310 --> 00:27:16.630
Yeah.
是啊。

617
00:27:16.630 --> 00:27:17.350
And you're like, okay.
然后你会觉得，好吧。

618
00:27:17.650 --> 00:27:18.330
Okay, fine.
好吧，行吧。

619
00:27:18.850 --> 00:27:23.630
Yeah, I think it is just that thing where Roy just, he just kind of doesn't see her.
是啊，我觉得这就是罗伊根本没把她放在心上的那种表现。

620
00:27:23.990 --> 00:27:27.710
He tried, but they're just not meant to be together.
他努力过，但他们注定不合适。

621
00:27:28.470 --> 00:27:34.430
Now, Dwight and Michael have arrived incredibly early to the party.
现在，德怀特和迈克尔早早地就到了聚会现场。

622
00:27:35.070 --> 00:27:40.670
There are catering vans and guys carrying in flowers.
现场有餐饮车，还有人在搬运花卉。

623
00:27:40.710 --> 00:27:44.930
Dwight realizes pretty quickly that Michael is dressed like the servants.
德怀特很快就意识到迈克尔穿得像个仆人。

624
00:27:45.190 --> 00:27:46.350
That's what he calls them.
他是这么称呼他们的。

625
00:27:46.910 --> 00:27:47.050
Yeah.
是啊。

626
00:27:47.050 --> 00:27:50.790
Um, and then they, of course, have to change clothes in the driveway.
嗯，然后他们当然得在车道上换衣服。

627
00:27:51.010 --> 00:27:53.070
And once again, we see Dwight's belly.
我们又一次看到了德怀特的肚子。

628
00:27:53.470 --> 00:27:54.550
Someone track that.
谁来统计一下吧。

629
00:27:54.750 --> 00:27:57.590
How many plants die and how many times do we see Dwight's belly?
到底有多少盆栽死掉，以及我们一共看到了多少次德怀特的肚子？

630
00:27:58.530 --> 00:28:05.390
Well, I love it that Michael says only good friends arrive early to a party.
我喜欢迈克尔说的那句，只有好朋友才会早到聚会。

631
00:28:05.670 --> 00:28:09.790
So the best way to become a good friend is to come early.
所以成为好朋友的最佳方式就是早点到。

632
00:28:10.190 --> 00:28:10.750
Yeah.
是啊。

633
00:28:11.070 --> 00:28:12.170
That's what you do.
这就是你要做的。

634
00:28:12.310 --> 00:28:13.270
That's his strategy.
这就是他的策略。

635
00:28:13.610 --> 00:28:17.690
His strategy is to be the first ones there and the last ones to leave.
他的策略就是做第一个到场、最后一个离开的人。

636
00:28:18.430 --> 00:28:20.370
And then you're going to love him.
这样你就会喜欢他了。

637
00:28:20.670 --> 00:28:22.970
You know, that reminds me of Ellie Kemper.
你知道吗，这让我想起了艾莉·坎伯。

638
00:28:23.190 --> 00:28:26.910
You know, Ellie Kemper had a rule to always be the last person at a party.
你知道，艾莉·坎伯有个规矩，就是永远要做聚会上最后一个走的人。

639
00:28:27.090 --> 00:28:27.810
I know.
我知道。

640
00:28:28.530 --> 00:28:29.890
And she is fun.
她很有趣。

641
00:28:30.010 --> 00:28:31.930
And you sort of adopted that with her.
你好像也跟她学了这一套。

642
00:28:32.130 --> 00:28:38.430
Yeah, because she told me that once and I was like, oh, I'm always the first one at a party.
是啊，因为她有次告诉了我，我就说，哦，我总是聚会上第一个到的。

643
00:28:38.430 --> 00:28:40.650
I like to come in the early part.
我喜欢早点去。

644
00:28:40.650 --> 00:28:41.630
And here's why.
原因如下。

645
00:28:42.370 --> 00:28:47.310
I'm not going to come so early that you're just getting out of the shower, okay, and your house isn't ready.
我不会早到让你刚洗完澡，或者家里还没准备好。

646
00:28:47.450 --> 00:28:48.670
I like to get there early.
我喜欢早点到。

647
00:28:48.870 --> 00:28:56.010
I get my FaceTime with the host, you know, get to have a sort of meaningful conversation because they're not juggling a lot of people yet.
我可以和主人面对面交流，你知道，能进行一些有意义的对话，因为那时候他们还没忙着应付一大堆人。

648
00:28:56.230 --> 00:29:01.030
And then I'm there as everyone arrives and I get to chit chat with everyone.
然后当大家陆续到达时，我已经在那里了，可以和每个人闲聊。

649
00:29:01.290 --> 00:29:06.110
I feel overwhelmed when I enter a party and it's like two hours in.
如果我进入聚会时已经开始了两个小时，我会感到不知所措。

650
00:29:06.610 --> 00:29:07.850
I'm like, oh, my gosh.
我会觉得，天哪。

651
00:29:07.850 --> 00:29:10.630
It's like too much like instant party for me.
对我来说，这就像是那种瞬间爆发的派对，太过了。

652
00:29:11.350 --> 00:29:13.430
I need to ease into a party.
我需要慢慢进入派对状态。

653
00:29:13.630 --> 00:29:17.330
I need the population of the party to grow around me slowly.
我需要派对里的人数慢慢增加。

654
00:29:17.630 --> 00:29:20.390
I think this is your metaphor for life, though, Jenna.
不过珍娜，我觉得这正是你的人生隐喻。

655
00:29:20.530 --> 00:29:22.850
I feel like you need to ease into situations.
我觉得你需要慢慢适应各种情况。

656
00:29:23.250 --> 00:29:25.530
Yeah, well, I have a lot of social anxiety.
是啊，我有很严重的社交焦虑。

657
00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:30.410
So my way of navigating large social situations is to ease in.
所以我应对大型社交场合的方式就是慢慢融入。

658
00:29:30.530 --> 00:29:32.330
I don't like an instant crowd.
我不喜欢一上来就人山人海。

659
00:29:32.510 --> 00:29:33.930
I like the instant crowd.
我喜欢那种瞬间热闹的氛围。

660
00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:35.270
I want to jump in.
我想直接跳进去。

661
00:29:35.370 --> 00:29:36.610
I want the music thumping.
我想感受音乐的轰鸣。

662
00:29:36.610 --> 00:29:39.590
I want everyone to have had like a little bit of a cocktail.
我想让每个人都喝点鸡尾酒。

663
00:29:40.270 --> 00:29:42.010
The pressure's off on me.
这样我就没有压力了。

664
00:29:42.330 --> 00:29:46.070
I can just show up and just be part of the flow.
我可以随时出现，融入其中。

665
00:29:46.530 --> 00:29:47.790
You get there early.
你到得太早了。

666
00:29:48.090 --> 00:29:48.970
I don't know, Jenna.
我不知道，珍娜。

667
00:29:49.210 --> 00:29:51.710
You might get stuck in a conversation that goes on forever.
你可能会陷入一场没完没了的谈话中。

668
00:29:52.430 --> 00:29:53.650
Well, that happens.
嗯，那种事确实会发生。

669
00:29:53.770 --> 00:29:54.510
That happens.
确实会发生。

670
00:29:54.730 --> 00:29:55.610
I'll take it.
我认了。

671
00:29:55.790 --> 00:29:57.990
I'd rather do that than the other thing.
我宁愿那样也不愿做别的事。

672
00:29:58.130 --> 00:30:03.810
And also, if you come early and you chat with the host, if I start to get overwhelmed,
而且，如果你早点到，和主人聊聊天，如果我开始感到不知所措，

673
00:30:03.810 --> 00:30:07.550
if my anxiety gets too high, Irish exit.
如果我的焦虑感太高，我就直接溜走。

674
00:30:07.610 --> 00:30:08.790
I can leave.
我可以离开。

675
00:30:08.950 --> 00:30:09.970
You just fade out.
你只是悄悄消失了。

676
00:30:10.090 --> 00:30:10.770
But I was there.
但我确实去过。

677
00:30:10.890 --> 00:30:12.270
Everyone knows I was there, right?
大家都知道我去过，对吧？

678
00:30:12.470 --> 00:30:17.190
And then just the social sort of like obligation is completed.
然后社交义务就完成了。

679
00:30:17.770 --> 00:30:19.510
Do I sound like fun?
我听起来很有趣吗？

680
00:30:19.690 --> 00:30:20.690
You are fun.
你很有趣。

681
00:30:20.830 --> 00:30:22.350
You actually are a ton of fun.
你其实非常有趣。

682
00:30:22.370 --> 00:30:23.010
I am fun.
我很有趣。

683
00:30:23.070 --> 00:30:24.210
You're a ton of fun.
你真的非常有趣。

684
00:30:24.470 --> 00:30:24.870
I am.
我是。

685
00:30:24.970 --> 00:30:26.610
It's just so fascinating to me.
这对我来说太迷人了。

686
00:30:26.770 --> 00:30:30.270
You and I have all of these core things that are so the same.
你和我有很多核心方面都非常相似。

687
00:30:30.450 --> 00:30:33.910
And then all of our social stuff is completely different.
但我们在社交方面却完全不同。

688
00:30:34.730 --> 00:30:35.770
It's so true.
确实如此。

689
00:30:35.770 --> 00:30:40.290
I always say Angela's house is like an episode of Three's Company.
我总是说安吉拉的家就像《三人行》的一集。

690
00:30:40.650 --> 00:30:44.190
There's just people coming through the door randomly at all times.
总有人随时随地随机地从门口进来。

691
00:30:45.150 --> 00:30:45.990
It's true.
是真的。

692
00:30:46.230 --> 00:30:47.350
I'm just like, come on in.
我就是那种，进来吧。

693
00:30:47.570 --> 00:30:48.510
I'm out back.
我在后院。

694
00:30:48.650 --> 00:30:49.610
Come down the driveway.
顺着车道走过来就行。

695
00:30:49.970 --> 00:30:50.530
Whatever.
随便吧。

696
00:30:50.850 --> 00:30:52.550
It's like your neighbor, your contractor.
就像你的邻居，你的承包商。

697
00:30:52.910 --> 00:30:53.910
I don't know.
我不知道。

698
00:30:54.170 --> 00:30:55.450
Literally anyone.
真的是任何人。

699
00:30:56.390 --> 00:30:57.530
Coming on over.
都过来。

700
00:30:58.870 --> 00:31:00.070
Creed comes with his guitar.
克里德还会带着他的吉他来。

701
00:31:00.390 --> 00:31:00.970
I know.
我知道。

702
00:31:01.310 --> 00:31:03.230
And I'm like, make an appointment.
我就说，预约一下吧。

703
00:31:03.530 --> 00:31:04.610
Make an appointment.
预约一下。

704
00:31:04.610 --> 00:31:06.210
Show up on time.
准时到场。

705
00:31:06.410 --> 00:31:09.030
I need to ready myself for the social interaction.
我得为社交互动做好心理准备。

706
00:31:10.550 --> 00:31:11.030
Okay.
好吧。

707
00:31:11.050 --> 00:31:14.170
So now the whole gang is arriving to Poor Richard's.
现在整帮人都到了“可怜理查”酒吧。

708
00:31:14.230 --> 00:31:17.830
And I have a little bit of Poor Richard's trivia, Jenna.
珍娜，我这儿还有点关于“可怜理查”的小知识。

709
00:31:18.490 --> 00:31:22.070
Oh, is this about the real Poor Richard's?
哦，是关于现实中那家“可怜理查”的吗？

710
00:31:22.130 --> 00:31:23.810
Because we had two people write in.
因为有两位听众写信问了。

711
00:31:23.930 --> 00:31:25.650
Lucas Bundros and Andrew L.
卢卡斯·邦德罗斯和安德鲁·L。

712
00:31:25.810 --> 00:31:29.170
said, is Poor Richard's a real pub that people can go to today?
他们问，“可怜理查”是现实中人们现在还能去的一家酒吧吗？

713
00:31:29.310 --> 00:31:30.450
And if so, where is it?
如果是的话，它在哪儿？

714
00:31:30.650 --> 00:31:32.430
Yes, it is a real pub.
是的，它确实是一家真实存在的酒吧。

715
00:31:32.430 --> 00:31:34.770
And it is in Scranton, Pennsylvania.
它位于宾夕法尼亚州的斯克兰顿。

716
00:31:35.490 --> 00:31:37.930
And here's the thing that was kind of interesting, Jenna.
珍娜，有件事挺有意思的。

717
00:31:38.390 --> 00:31:41.830
Where we shot in Los Angeles was attached to a bowling alley, right?
我们在洛杉矶拍摄的地方是连着一家保龄球馆的，对吧？

718
00:31:42.290 --> 00:31:42.730
Yep.
没错。

719
00:31:43.130 --> 00:31:44.530
So is Poor Richard's.
“可怜理查”也是这样。

720
00:31:44.630 --> 00:31:46.150
It is not a standalone bar.
它不是一家独立的酒吧。

721
00:31:46.950 --> 00:31:49.110
It is part of a bowling alley.
它是保龄球馆的一部分。

722
00:31:49.590 --> 00:31:50.050
Yes.
是的。

723
00:31:51.390 --> 00:31:53.610
Is the bowling alley called Poor Richard's?
那家保龄球馆也叫“可怜理查”吗？

724
00:31:53.630 --> 00:31:53.910
No.
不叫。

725
00:31:54.130 --> 00:31:55.870
The bowling alley is its own thing.
保龄球馆有它自己的名字。

726
00:31:56.190 --> 00:31:57.210
Here's the cool thing.
酷的地方在于。

727
00:31:57.430 --> 00:32:00.970
Poor Richard's actually does have a door that goes into the bar from the outside.
“可怜理查”确实有一扇门可以从外面直接进入酒吧。

728
00:32:01.490 --> 00:32:05.750
But when you go into the bar, there's a whole section of it that just opens out into the bowling alley.
但当你走进酒吧，里面有一大片区域是直接通向保龄球馆的。

729
00:32:06.310 --> 00:32:06.770
Wow.
哇。

730
00:32:06.970 --> 00:32:07.170
Yeah.
是啊。

731
00:32:07.350 --> 00:32:09.050
That's exactly what it's like at Pickwick.
这和皮克威克的情况一模一样。

732
00:32:09.050 --> 00:32:09.630
Yeah.
没错。

733
00:32:09.990 --> 00:32:19.330
And right next to the door to go inside is like an old-timey-looking wooden plaque thing that says Poor Richard's.
而且在入口旁边，有一个看起来很有年代感的木制牌匾，上面写着“可怜理查”。

734
00:32:19.590 --> 00:32:21.870
And I have a photo I took by it.
我还在那儿拍了张照片。

735
00:32:21.970 --> 00:32:25.690
Actually, in 2018, my husband and I were randomly driving through Pennsylvania.
其实在2018年，我和我丈夫开车路过宾夕法尼亚州。

736
00:32:26.250 --> 00:32:32.870
And I was like, oh, my God, it's a good hour and a half out of the way, but let's go to Scranton.
我就说，天哪，虽然要绕路一个半小时，但我们去趟斯克兰顿吧。

737
00:32:32.970 --> 00:32:34.690
And we drove to Scranton, and we drove all around.
于是我们开车去了斯克兰顿，到处转了转。

738
00:32:34.690 --> 00:32:36.770
And I said, let's go to Poor Richard's and grab a beer.
我说，咱们去“可怜理查”喝杯啤酒吧。

739
00:32:36.910 --> 00:32:38.430
But it was closed.
结果它关门了。

740
00:32:39.250 --> 00:32:40.050
Oh, no.
哦，不。

741
00:32:40.490 --> 00:32:40.810
I know.
我知道。

742
00:32:40.930 --> 00:32:43.150
So I took all these pictures by the plaque.
所以我只能在那块牌匾旁边拍了好多照片。

743
00:32:43.350 --> 00:32:50.730
But years and years ago, 2017, I was there, and I went inside Poor Richard's with Brian Baumgartner.
但在很多年前，2017年的时候，我去过那里，还和布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳一起进了“可怜理查”。

744
00:32:50.930 --> 00:32:52.090
What was that like?
那感觉怎么样？

745
00:32:52.330 --> 00:32:53.670
It was such a blaSt.
简直太棒了。

746
00:32:54.330 --> 00:32:59.610
We just drank beer and hung out with the folks from Scranton who were all so nice.
我们就在那儿喝啤酒，和斯克兰顿当地人聊天，他们人都特别好。

747
00:32:59.670 --> 00:33:02.250
And I just love that town.
我真的很喜欢那个小镇。

748
00:33:03.210 --> 00:33:04.270
Yeah, me too.
我也是。

749
00:33:04.530 --> 00:33:07.350
I've only been there the one time, but it was so great.
我只去过那一次，但真的太棒了。

750
00:33:07.530 --> 00:33:08.590
It's so fun.
太有意思了。

751
00:33:09.030 --> 00:33:12.350
But, yeah, I have some great photos from Poor Richard's.
不过，没错，我在“穷理查”酒吧拍了一些很棒的照片。

752
00:33:12.450 --> 00:33:17.770
But, yeah, you guys, families are bowling, and then folks are in the bar just right there on the side.
但是，伙计们，当时有家庭在打保龄球，旁边就是酒吧。

753
00:33:18.050 --> 00:33:22.830
But I want to tell you guys, if you go to Poor Richard's, here's something that you would never think.
但我得告诉你们，如果你们去“穷理查”，有一件事你们绝对想不到。

754
00:33:22.830 --> 00:33:26.510
They have so many different types of French fries.
他们有各种各样的炸薯条。

755
00:33:26.710 --> 00:33:27.430
Tell me more.
多跟我说说。

756
00:33:27.630 --> 00:33:29.370
You can get regular French fries.
你可以点普通的炸薯条。

757
00:33:29.590 --> 00:33:31.210
You can get French fries with gravy.
可以点肉汁炸薯条。

758
00:33:31.410 --> 00:33:32.770
French fries with cheese.
芝士炸薯条。

759
00:33:33.070 --> 00:33:34.810
French fries with cheese and gravy.
芝士肉汁炸薯条。

760
00:33:35.390 --> 00:33:36.470
Chili cheese fries.
辣酱芝士薯条。

761
00:33:37.070 --> 00:33:41.730
Devil fries, which are smothered in hot or mild sauce with your choice of cheese.
恶魔薯条，上面淋着特辣或微辣酱汁，还可以自选芝士。

762
00:33:42.030 --> 00:33:47.050
Pizza fries, which have garlic Parmesan seasoned fries with pizza cheese and marinara.
披萨薯条，用蒜香帕尔马干酪调味，配上披萨芝士和番茄酱。

763
00:33:47.050 --> 00:33:56.990
Bacon cheddar ranch fries, spicy curly fries, or sweet potato fries with salted caramel and marshmallow glaze.
培根切达干酪牧场风味薯条、香辣卷曲薯条，或者配有海盐焦糖和棉花糖糖衣的红薯条。

764
00:33:58.610 --> 00:34:01.370
Did you order any fries when you were there with Brian?
你和布莱恩去那儿的时候点薯条了吗？

765
00:34:01.650 --> 00:34:02.250
I did.
点了。

766
00:34:02.730 --> 00:34:03.590
Which ones?
点的哪种？

767
00:34:03.850 --> 00:34:05.010
I got the plain ones.
我点的原味的。

768
00:34:05.130 --> 00:34:07.430
I didn't realize they had so many others.
我都没意识到他们还有这么多其他口味。

769
00:34:07.670 --> 00:34:08.730
They were like, what would you like?
当时他们问我想要什么。

770
00:34:08.730 --> 00:34:11.530
I was like, I'll have some French fries, you know, because I was just trying to snack.
我说，给我来点炸薯条吧，你知道的，我当时只是想随便吃点零食。

771
00:34:11.530 --> 00:34:16.870
Had I known, I think I would have hit up those bacon cheddar ranch fries.
要是早知道，我想我肯定会点那个培根切达干酪牧场风味薯条。

772
00:34:18.410 --> 00:34:18.850
Wow.
哇。

773
00:34:19.130 --> 00:34:19.470
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

774
00:34:20.230 --> 00:34:22.070
I see a road trip in our future.
我预见我们未来会有一次公路旅行。

775
00:34:22.370 --> 00:34:23.890
Oh, good Lord.
噢，天哪。

776
00:34:23.890 --> 00:34:25.170
I would love that.
我很乐意。

777
00:34:25.390 --> 00:34:27.090
You and I driving through Scranton?
你和我开车穿过斯克兰顿？

778
00:34:27.830 --> 00:34:28.270
Ugh.
呃。

779
00:34:28.450 --> 00:34:29.130
Come on.
拜托。

780
00:34:29.590 --> 00:34:30.970
We have to make that happen.
我们一定要实现它。

781
00:34:31.130 --> 00:34:31.990
We've got a liSt.
我们有个清单。

782
00:34:32.190 --> 00:34:33.010
We've got a liSt.
我们有个清单。

783
00:34:33.210 --> 00:34:34.070
We've got a bucket liSt.
我们有个遗愿清单。

784
00:34:34.450 --> 00:34:36.770
You guys, you can find out more about Poor Richard's.
伙计们，你们可以去了解更多关于“穷理查”的信息。

785
00:34:36.770 --> 00:34:39.410
You can go to poorrichardspub.net.
可以访问 poorrichardspub.net。

786
00:34:40.390 --> 00:34:47.630
Well, the gang all sits around the table, and they're having some drinks, and Pam asks
当时大家伙儿都围坐在桌边喝酒，帕姆问了

787
00:34:47.630 --> 00:34:49.230
Kevin about his wedding plans.
凯文关于他婚礼的计划。

788
00:34:49.730 --> 00:34:50.250
Yeah.
没错。

789
00:34:50.370 --> 00:34:52.270
And he's like, yeah, we set a date.
他说，是啊，我们定好日子了。

790
00:34:52.450 --> 00:34:54.110
Everyone's so excited to hear more.
大家都特别兴奋，想听听细节。

791
00:34:54.290 --> 00:34:56.370
And then he's like, you know what?
然后他说，你们知道吗？

792
00:34:56.430 --> 00:34:58.850
It's complicated, and I'd really like some space.
这事儿挺复杂的，我真的需要一点空间。

793
00:34:58.890 --> 00:34:59.190
Yeah.
是啊。

794
00:34:59.270 --> 00:35:00.690
I need some space on this.
在这件事上我需要一点空间。

795
00:35:01.210 --> 00:35:01.550
What?
什么？

796
00:35:01.550 --> 00:35:09.350
At seven minutes, three seconds, there is a fantastic close-up of Brian's tiny curled
在七分零三秒的时候，有一个布莱恩头部两侧卷发的小特写，

797
00:35:09.350 --> 00:35:11.310
hair on either side of his head.
非常精彩。

798
00:35:11.970 --> 00:35:12.530
Oh.
噢。

799
00:35:13.210 --> 00:35:13.770
Yes.
没错。

800
