I'm trying to do physical exercise three to four days a week and I've been eating really
我正尝试每周锻炼三到四次，而且吃得也

1127
00:49:16.860 --> 00:49:20.160
good, but I had this slow moment with the box of cheddar crackers.
很健康，但面对那盒切达饼干时，我还是没把持住。

1128
00:49:21.340 --> 00:49:22.220
I don't know.
我不知道。

1129
00:49:22.220 --> 00:49:27.400
Sometimes you need to be okay, not being okay, right?
有时候你需要接受自己的不完美，对吧？

1130
00:49:27.900 --> 00:49:29.320
Lady, who are you talking to?
大姐，你这是在跟谁说话呢？

1131
00:49:29.880 --> 00:49:32.520
I got nothing but love for you with all of that.
对于你说的这些，我只有满满的理解。

1132
00:49:32.700 --> 00:49:36.880
I mean, do you remember that night where it was like 11 o'clock at night and I was like,
我是说，你还记得那天晚上大概11点的时候，我说，

1133
00:49:36.960 --> 00:49:39.000
well, I guess someone needs a piece of chocolate pie.
好吧，看来有人需要来块巧克力派了。

1134
00:49:39.300 --> 00:49:40.420
I guess that person's me.
那个人应该就是我。

1135
00:49:41.360 --> 00:49:42.400
Everyone's gone to bed.
大家都睡了。

1136
00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:44.200
I'm not even going to put it on a plate.
我甚至懒得把它装进盘子里。

1137
00:49:44.440 --> 00:49:50.060
I'm going to stand inside the fridge and just have a fork and just carve at it.
我就站在冰箱前，拿把叉子直接挖着吃。

1138
00:49:53.100 --> 00:49:58.740
I do remember because you sent me a video message of yourself eating the pie from the fridge.
我当然记得，因为你当时给我发了个视频，拍着你自己站在冰箱前吃派的样子。

1139
00:49:59.460 --> 00:50:01.900
And I'll tell you what, it made me feel better.
我跟你说，那让我感觉好多了。

1140
00:50:02.100 --> 00:50:02.780
There you go.
这就对了。

1141
00:50:03.500 --> 00:50:04.360
There you go.
这就对了。

1142
00:50:04.500 --> 00:50:05.940
Okay, wait, where are we?
好了，等等，我们讲到哪了？

1143
00:50:05.940 --> 00:50:25.300
Where we are is that Jan and Michael have arrived to the party and they're outside and Jan wants Michael to sign some papers waiving his right to sue Dunder Mifflin in the event that their relationship in his mind or in reality interferes with work.
我们讲到简和迈克尔已经到了派对现场，他们正在外面，简想让迈克尔签一些文件，放弃他在他们的关系（无论是在他心里还是现实中）影响工作时起诉邓德·米夫林的权利。

1144
00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:32.520
I have to tell you, I laughed so hard when she was digging in her trunk and he said, what you looking for?
我得告诉你，当她在后备箱里翻找时，迈克尔问她在找什么，我笑得不行。

1145
00:50:32.700 --> 00:50:33.560
You bring a dip?
你带蘸酱了吗？

1146
00:50:34.900 --> 00:50:39.520
Like somewhere in Michael's mind, you go to a party, you bring a dip.
在迈克尔的脑回路里，去参加派对就得带蘸酱。

1147
00:50:39.740 --> 00:50:41.440
No matter what party, you bring a dip.
不管什么派对，你都得带蘸酱。

1148
00:50:41.660 --> 00:50:44.680
He's like, everybody must have brought a dip, right?
他觉得，每个人肯定都带了蘸酱，对吧？

1149
00:50:46.460 --> 00:50:49.180
Also, I cannot get enough of Jan and Michael.
还有，我真是看不够简和迈克尔的戏份。

1150
00:50:49.500 --> 00:50:49.920
I know.
我知道。

1151
00:50:50.140 --> 00:50:51.280
I love this relationship.
我太爱这段关系了。

1152
00:50:51.280 --> 00:50:53.560
I love Melora Harden so much.
我太喜欢梅洛拉·哈登了。

1153
00:50:53.720 --> 00:50:54.880
She's so phenomenal.
她真是太棒了。

1154
00:50:55.560 --> 00:50:56.660
God, she's good.
天哪，她演得真好。

1155
00:50:56.880 --> 00:51:02.980
Well, you know, she has this amazing talking head where she's like, hey, yeah, this is a calculated risk, you know, upside.
你知道，她有个很棒的访谈片段，她说，嘿，没错，这是一场经过计算的冒险，你知道，好处是……

1156
00:51:03.580 --> 00:51:08.260
I'm going to fall deeply in love and have babies and normalcy, no more self-loathing.
我会坠入爱河，生儿育女，过上正常的生活，不再自我厌恶。

1157
00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:12.640
Downside, she collapses in on herself like a dying star, right?
坏处是，她会像一颗垂死的恒星一样自我坍塌，对吧？

1158
00:51:13.660 --> 00:51:18.560
So in the deleted scenes, she has a much longer talking head.
在删减片段里，她有一段长得多的访谈。

1159
00:51:18.760 --> 00:51:20.380
They really trim this down.
他们真的剪掉了很多。

1160
00:51:20.600 --> 00:51:25.540
And lady, she overshares so much.
天哪，她分享的私事太多了。

1161
00:51:25.740 --> 00:51:28.180
Like it's so uncomfortable to watch.
看得让人特别尴尬。

1162
00:51:28.640 --> 00:51:30.020
What does she say?
她说了什么？

1163
00:51:30.280 --> 00:51:33.080
I mean, she talks about past relationships.
我是说，她谈到了过去的感情经历。

1164
00:51:33.080 --> 00:51:37.200
She was like, well, I guess one good thing is I orgasm really easily.
她说，嗯，我想好的一点是，我很容易达到高潮。

1165
00:51:37.700 --> 00:51:40.760
So she really overshares.
所以她真的分享得太多了。

1166
00:51:41.420 --> 00:51:45.440
And I was like, oh, my God, I see why they deleted it.
当时我就想，天哪，我明白他们为什么要删掉这段了。

1167
00:51:45.600 --> 00:51:51.300
But it really, really does show you where Jan is at, her mental space.
但这确实非常直观地展现了简当时的心理状态。

1168
00:51:52.400 --> 00:51:58.960
Well, as soon as he walks in the door with Jan, they run in to David Wallace.
当他带着简走进门时，他们正好撞见了大卫·华莱士。

1169
00:52:06.520 --> 00:52:10.900
He doesn't say Jan and I are dating.
他没有说简和我在约会。

1170
00:52:11.220 --> 00:52:12.920
First of all, he doesn't need to say that.
首先，他没必要说这个。

1171
00:52:13.080 --> 00:52:15.720
He doesn't need to clarify their relationship.
他不需要去澄清他们的关系。

1172
00:52:15.720 --> 00:52:17.340
But he's so excited.
但他太兴奋了。

1173
00:52:17.340 --> 00:52:20.600
And he always refers to them as lovers.
而且他总是称呼对方为“爱人”。

1174
00:52:20.800 --> 00:52:25.660
And you guys, I don't know if you guys have ever had people like this in your life.
你们呢，我不知道你们生活中是否遇到过这样的人。

1175
00:52:25.800 --> 00:52:31.960
But I know a couple who, when they talk about each other, they refer to each other as their lover.
但我认识一对情侣，他们谈起对方时，总是称呼对方为“我的爱人”。

1176
00:52:32.880 --> 00:52:36.620
And it makes me so uncomfortable every time.
每次听到都让我觉得特别尴尬。

1177
00:52:37.200 --> 00:52:37.860
Every time.
每一次都是。

1178
00:52:37.860 --> 00:52:42.160
I remember when they got engaged, we were like, oh, tell us your engagement story.
我记得他们订婚的时候，我们说，噢，给我们讲讲你们的求婚故事吧。

1179
00:52:42.720 --> 00:52:46.260
And they were like, well, we said to each other, you know what?
他们说，嗯，我们当时对彼此说，你知道吗？

1180
00:52:46.520 --> 00:52:47.740
You are my lover.
你是我的爱人。

1181
00:52:48.440 --> 00:52:49.560
You are my friend.
你是我的朋友。

1182
00:52:49.840 --> 00:52:52.200
It's always, they always bring it up.
总是这样，他们总是会提起这个词。

1183
00:52:52.860 --> 00:52:53.820
Is it me and Lee?
是指我和李吗？

1184
00:52:54.140 --> 00:52:54.380
No.
不是。

1185
00:52:56.520 --> 00:52:58.800
And why are you saying you don't like it that I say that?
那你为什么说你不喜欢我那样说？

1186
00:52:59.240 --> 00:53:02.060
That Lee and I refer to one another as lovers.
说我和李互称对方为爱人。

1187
00:53:02.160 --> 00:53:02.260
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1188
00:53:02.260 --> 00:53:02.860
I can't.
我受不了了。

1189
00:53:02.880 --> 00:53:03.840
I want to do it now.
我现在就想这么干。

1190
00:53:04.000 --> 00:53:04.220
Oh.
噢。

1191
00:53:04.320 --> 00:53:08.760
The next time I go to a party, I'm going to introduce Lee and I as lovers.
下次我去参加聚会时，我要介绍我和李是“爱人”。

1192
00:53:08.920 --> 00:53:09.180
You know what?
你知道吗？

1193
00:53:09.360 --> 00:53:10.060
This is my lover, Lee.
这是我的爱人，李。

1194
00:53:10.240 --> 00:53:15.680
Show up really early when there's no one else to buffer your awkward conversation.
早点到场，那时候还没人能帮你化解尴尬的谈话。

1195
00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:17.720
And no one's had a drink yet.
而且还没人开始喝酒。

1196
00:53:17.720 --> 00:53:20.260
And be like, my lover and I are early.
然后说，我和我的爱人来早了。

1197
00:53:20.500 --> 00:53:23.220
And my lover and I brought Cheez-Its or whatever.
我和我的爱人带了芝士脆饼之类的东西。

1198
00:53:23.740 --> 00:53:25.680
We brought some bunny snack mix.
我们带了些兔子形状的零食。

1199
00:53:26.660 --> 00:53:29.380
My lover told me not to eat so many in the car.
我的爱人告诉我别在车里吃太多。

1200
00:53:29.620 --> 00:53:31.060
And I said, lover, you're silly.
我说，爱人，你真傻。

1201
00:53:31.060 --> 00:53:34.820
I can't wait to do this bit at my next party.
我迫不及待想在下次聚会上玩这个梗了。

1202
00:53:35.020 --> 00:53:36.700
Oh, it makes me so uncomfortable.
噢，这让我感到非常不自在。

1203
00:53:37.080 --> 00:53:40.820
So now we're, the party is going at David Wallace's house.
所以现在，聚会在大卫·华莱士家里进行着。

1204
00:53:41.000 --> 00:53:47.580
And we just have what is possibly one of the most awkward conversations at a party.
我们刚刚经历了聚会上可能最尴尬的一段对话。

1205
00:53:48.020 --> 00:53:48.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1206
00:53:48.620 --> 00:53:50.300
Nine minutes, 52 seconds.
9分52秒。

1207
00:53:50.800 --> 00:53:52.540
Michael tries to hold Jan's hand.
迈克尔试图去牵简的手。

1208
00:53:52.680 --> 00:53:55.500
He's already, you know, as we said, called her his lover.
正如我们所说，他已经称呼她为他的爱人了。

1209
00:53:55.740 --> 00:53:56.960
Then he tries to hold her hand.
然后他试着去牵她的手。

1210
00:53:57.120 --> 00:53:58.000
She won't hold his hand.
她不让他牵。

1211
00:53:58.000 --> 00:54:00.400
Then he blows in her face.
接着他对着她的脸吹气。

1212
00:54:01.080 --> 00:54:03.000
Then he asks for an appetizer.
然后他要点开胃菜。

1213
00:54:03.240 --> 00:54:05.220
Wants to know if they have any bagel bites.
想知道他们有没有贝果小食。

1214
00:54:06.440 --> 00:54:06.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1215
00:54:06.700 --> 00:54:08.980
Then Dwight asks for the square footage of the house.
然后德怀特问这房子的平方英尺是多少。

1216
00:54:09.140 --> 00:54:10.480
Then Michael's like, that's inappropriate.
接着迈克尔说，这太不礼貌了。

1217
00:54:10.880 --> 00:54:12.580
How much does this house cost?
这房子值多少钱？

1218
00:54:13.320 --> 00:54:17.880
And then doesn't Jim, like, do like a spit take with his drink?
然后吉姆是不是喷了一口饮料？

1219
00:54:18.400 --> 00:54:19.360
Let me tell you something.
我跟你说件事。

1220
00:54:19.360 --> 00:54:24.220
I was having a cup of tea while I was watching this episode, and I happened to be taking a sip
我在看这一集的时候正好在喝茶，我刚好喝了一口

1221
00:54:24.220 --> 00:54:25.280
right at this moment.
就在那一刻。

1222
00:54:26.180 --> 00:54:32.120
And Jim and I simultaneously spit into our cups from that line.
听到那句台词，我和吉姆同时把茶喷回了杯子里。

1223
00:54:32.280 --> 00:54:35.420
That line made me laugh out loud.
那句台词让我大笑出声。

1224
00:54:35.740 --> 00:54:36.400
I know.
我知道。

1225
00:54:36.540 --> 00:54:37.880
It's so awkward.
太尴尬了。

1226
00:54:37.880 --> 00:54:43.700
And it sends Dwight now on this crazy journey of checking out every nook and cranny of their house.
这让德怀特开始了一段疯狂的旅程，去查看他们房子的每一个角落。

1227
00:54:44.300 --> 00:54:44.800
Yes.
没错。

1228
00:54:45.060 --> 00:54:49.520
And this is also where Karen is going to start her little prank on Jim.
这也是凯伦开始对吉姆搞恶作剧的地方。

1229
00:54:50.360 --> 00:54:53.220
She says to Jim, do you see that guy over there?
她对吉姆说，你看到那边那个人了吗？

1230
00:54:53.420 --> 00:54:58.360
Because I just think you should know we used to date and it didn't end well.
我觉得你应该知道，我们曾经约会过，而且结局不太好。

1231
00:54:58.880 --> 00:55:00.520
And Jim is like, oh.
吉姆说，噢。

1232
00:55:01.100 --> 00:55:02.440
I didn't like this prank.
我不喜欢这个恶作剧。

1233
00:55:02.620 --> 00:55:03.800
I didn't like the storyline.
我不喜欢这个剧情线。

1234
00:55:04.620 --> 00:55:05.580
Tell me more.
多跟我说说。

1235
00:55:06.200 --> 00:55:10.400
Well, I mean, I think it's passive aggressive.
嗯，我觉得这有点消极攻击。

1236
00:55:11.220 --> 00:55:19.900
I think Karen is maybe still a little stung by the fact that Jim dated Pam and the way she found
我觉得凯伦可能还是因为吉姆和帕姆约会过，以及她发现这件事的方式

1237
00:55:19.900 --> 00:55:20.740
out about it.
而感到有些受伤。

1238
00:55:21.000 --> 00:55:26.360
And I feel like this is her kind of playful way to make light of it, although it's not
我觉得这是她一种戏谑的方式来淡化这件事，尽管她心里并不觉得轻松，

1239
00:55:26.360 --> 00:55:30.860
something that she feels light about because they've had all these late night talks.
因为他们有过那么多深夜长谈。

1240
00:55:30.860 --> 00:55:38.880
But it's her sort of playful way of, I don't know, kind of jabbing him about it.
但这算是她一种戏谑的方式，我不知道，算是以此来刺他一下吧。

1241
00:55:39.400 --> 00:55:39.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1242
00:55:39.960 --> 00:55:44.980
And it feels a little sad and a little desperate to me, Karen.
我觉得这让凯伦看起来有点可悲，也有点绝望。

1243
00:55:45.280 --> 00:55:45.560
Oh!
噢！

1244
00:55:46.840 --> 00:55:47.440
Wow.
哇。

1245
00:55:47.720 --> 00:55:48.840
You said it.
你说了。

1246
00:55:48.920 --> 00:55:49.600
I said it.
我说了。

1247
00:55:49.780 --> 00:55:52.520
Well, should we talk about this scene with the scotch?
好吧，我们要聊聊那个喝苏格兰威士忌的场景吗？

1248
00:55:52.800 --> 00:55:53.880
Oh, God.
天哪。

1249
00:55:53.880 --> 00:55:55.200
It is so good.
那段太棒了。

1250
00:55:55.560 --> 00:55:59.340
There's wonderful moments in the deleted scenes, too.
删减片段里也有很精彩的时刻。

1251
00:55:59.340 --> 00:56:00.300
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1252
00:56:01.300 --> 00:56:09.420
Well, I have to say, when Steve takes a sip of this scotch, which David tells us was gifted
好吧，我不得不说，当史蒂夫喝下这口苏格兰威士忌时——大卫告诉我们这是李·艾柯卡送给他的礼物——

1253
00:56:09.420 --> 00:56:13.520
to him by Lee Iacocca, Steve starts coughing.
史蒂夫开始咳嗽。

1254
00:56:14.160 --> 00:56:20.040
And it is some of the best liquor coughing I've ever seen in a performance.
那是我在表演中见过最棒的喝酒咳嗽戏了。

1255
00:56:20.060 --> 00:56:21.420
It was so real.
演得太真实了。

1256
00:56:21.600 --> 00:56:25.960
And it's so amazing, too, because there's a great moment in the bloopers where he's like
而且非常精彩，因为在花絮里有个很棒的瞬间，他说

1257
00:56:25.960 --> 00:56:27.560
over the gums and through the lips.
越过牙龈，穿过嘴唇。

1258
00:56:27.560 --> 00:56:35.520
He is not understanding the magnitude of a 20-year-old scotch given by this amazing man who he thinks
他根本没意识到这瓶由那位他以为发明了德罗宁跑车的传奇人物所赠的20年陈酿苏格兰威士忌有多珍贵。

1259
00:56:35.520 --> 00:56:36.820
discovered the DeLorean.
没错。

1260
00:56:38.120 --> 00:56:38.640
Yes.
是的。

1261
00:56:38.940 --> 00:56:40.060
All of it is wrong.
全搞错了。

1262
00:56:40.240 --> 00:56:41.360
All of it is wrong.
全搞错了。

1263
00:56:41.760 --> 00:56:46.880
We had a few people write in about that joke, and they were like, I don't understand the
我们收到了一些关于那个笑话的来信，他们说，我不明白关于李·艾柯卡和德罗宁跑车的笑话。

1264
00:56:46.880 --> 00:56:49.260
joke about Lee Iacocca and the DeLorean.
这纯粹是迈克尔的问题。

1265
00:56:49.540 --> 00:56:51.980
And this is just a matter of Michael.
他只是搞混了汽车业的高管。

1266
00:56:52.180 --> 00:56:55.740
He's just mixing up his automobile executives.
是的。

1267
00:56:56.180 --> 00:56:56.640
Yes.
这就是典型的迈克尔，他能记住一部分，剩下的全搞错。

1268
00:56:56.800 --> 00:57:00.540
This is classic Michael where he gets one part right and then the rest wrong.
没错。

1269
00:57:00.540 --> 00:57:01.540
Yes.
所以对于不知道的人，李·艾柯卡最出名的是开发了福特野马

1270
00:57:01.900 --> 00:57:07.960
So for anyone who doesn't know, Lee Iacocca was best known for developing the Ford Mustang
和平托汽车。

1271
00:57:07.960 --> 00:57:09.840
and the Pinto cars.
他曾在福特工作，后来去了克莱斯勒。

1272
00:57:10.060 --> 00:57:12.980
He worked for Ford, but then he went on to work at Chrysler.
他简直就是汽车业的传奇高管。

